data: {"id":"chatcmpl-dde1abc0-d722-43c0-bc55-6df37dad804e","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795555059,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Conflict detection strategy requires re-evaluation. A single transaction with numerous read and range operations and the potential for concurrent commits necessitates immediate conflict resolution during the read process. If a conflict is detected mid-transaction based on the `lastWriteCommitSeq`, the transaction can be immediately marked as conflicted, avoiding costly final checks. This simplifies the approach to handle conflict scenarios.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-dde1abc0-d722-43c0-bc55-6df37dad804e","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795555059,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"A single `READ` or `RANGE` operation can cause the transaction to be immediately marked as conflicted.  The `alreadyConflicted` flag avoids appending more read keys/ranges once a conflict is detected. The `lastWriteCommitSeq` map remains the sole source of conflict detection: a commit after a `READ`/`RANGE` operation can cause a conflict. Verification is underway for the correctness of the `lastWriteCommitSeq` map in all scenarios.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-dde1abc0-d722-43c0-bc55-6df37dad804e","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795555059,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Considering R22 and the implications for conflict determination, a key insight is that only committed transactions contribute to conflict detection; aborted transactions are excluded. Thus, `lastWriteCommitSeq` is updated exclusively with keys from committed transactions' write lists. This also implies that if a transaction writes and then reads the same key, and no other transaction modifies the key, there's no conflict during its commit.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-dde1abc0-d722-43c0-bc55-6df37dad804e","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795555059,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Rereading the conflict definition (R22), a crucial detail emerged: conflict detection only considers committed transactions' writes.  Focusing on a concurrent transaction `U`, the condition `uCommitSeq > T.beginCommitSeq` ensures `U`'s commit happened after `T` began.  Further analysis confirms a conflict only arises if `U` committed after `T.BEGIN` and before `T.COMMIT`, and if `U` wrote a key read or ranged by `T`. This confirms the `lastWriteCommitSeq` logic.  \n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

