data: {"id":"chatcmpl-dde1abc0-d722-43c0-bc55-6df37dad804e","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795555059,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Initial calculations indicate memory usage well within the 512MB limit, even with a high transaction volume and key count. The mutable AVL tree's memory footprint is efficiently managed due to in-place updates. The focus shifts to iteratively building the final state map during the recovery process to optimize memory further. The mutable AVL node is allocated as follows: a SnapNode of 40 bytes and the SeqNode, a mutable 40 bytes. The 20 MB of string is allocated during the final HashMap.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

